Approach: Check if lengths are equal, then concatenate string with itself (s + s) and verify if goal exists as a substring.

Time Complexity: O(n) — substring check on (s+s) takes linear time.

Space Complexity: O(n) — extra space used for concatenated string.

class Solution {
    public boolean rotateString(String s, String g) {
         if(s.length()!=g.length()){
            return false;
        }
        return (s+s).contains(g);
